[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AC-OCD003
TITLE: The spoken position matches the point-mass state
STATEMENT: >>>
When the pilot reports a position or includes a position in a call, the words shall describe the aircraft point-mass state at that moment, including the pattern leg when the aircraft is on one and the distance and direction when it is not. Acceptance is a concept in which a reader of the phrase log can tell the leg or the distance that the model occupied when the phrase was sent.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A phrase that names the wrong place is not a usable mock.
<<<
DAL: E
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Operational
VERIFICATION: Review
ASSUMPTIONS: The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.
